{"metadata":{"title":"ending","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV6endingAA9MXLEndingVSgvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ending"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLEnding","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/ending"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ending"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","text":"MXLEnding"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<ending>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/ending"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The multiple-ending bracket associated with this barline.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/ending":{"abstract":[{"text":"The multiple-ending bracket associated with this barline.","type":"text"}],"title":"ending","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/ending","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ending","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLEnding","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/ending"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}